WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.736
-Our first guest tonight
hosts "Alex Wagner Tonight"

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:06.372
Tuesdays through Fridays
at 9:00 p.m. on MSNBC.

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:07.406
Please welcome back to the show,

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:08.841
our friend Alex Wagner,
everybody.

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:11.544
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:21.554 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.457
Thank you for being here.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.926
-You got to do the live
coverage thing last night.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:28.194
-I sure did. Five hours.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.563
-Five hours. Well done.
Five hours.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.332
I feel like that
gives you a lot of time

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.433
to develop some takes on it.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:36.635
-Especially when they call
the election like an hour in.

00:00:36.635 --> 00:00:38.037
-An hour in.
-Yes.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:39.972
-This does seem like a night
that was maybe...

00:00:39.972 --> 00:00:42.575
bad for both of them.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.577
Do you feel like
there's anything to that?

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:47.213
-I'm a glass half full
kind of gal.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:49.582
Maybe good for both of them
or ultimately bad.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:52.284
I think it was...

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:53.820
I mean, it's bad for Trump

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.221
as far as the general election,
right?

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.823
-Yeah.
-It's very clear

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.624
that college-educated voters,

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:00.493
independents do not
like Donald Trump.

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:04.730
He attracts his base and repels
independents in equal measure.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.933
Um, you know,
I think for Joe Biden it is --

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.034
Are you talking about them?

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.135
You're talking
about Biden and...?

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.436
-No, I'm talking about
Haley and Trump.

00:01:10.436 --> 00:01:11.604
You'll have to excuse me.
-Sorry.

00:01:11.604 --> 00:01:13.506
My mind is on the general.
-[ Indistinct ]

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:14.807
-For Nikki Haley,

00:01:14.807 --> 00:01:18.744
like, it's good that
she did well among people

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:20.279
who actually aren't a huge part

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:22.215
of the Republican primary
electorate.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:24.216
It would be great if she could
make it to the general election,

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:25.418
but she's not going to.
-Yeah.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.153
-It was a bad night for her.

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.654
-And now, you know, again,

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:30.022
we saw him,
and we just showed a clip.

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:32.659
She came after him pretty hard
about his, uh,

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:33.993
electability problems
in a general.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:36.729
-Yes.
-Do you feel like her...

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.431
The rest of the field
before they dropped out,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.732
do you feel like
they made a mistake

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:42.335
not making that case earlier?
-Can I just say

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:45.504
just to put a fine point
on, like, criticizing Trump?

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:48.741
Yes, she makes a point
about his cognitive decline.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.610
She makes a point about
how he's not a kingmaker

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:52.845
in contested tight elections.

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.248
But there are a lot
of big elephants in the room

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.582
that she doesn't talk about.

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.117
Like, I don't know,
shredding the Constitution,

00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.819
saying he wants to be
a dictator on day one

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.187
and undermining democracy.
-Yeah.

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:03.356
-That stuff, like...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:03.356 --> 00:02:05.558
...I maintain...

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.560
she hasn't really gone
for the jugular.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.530
But, you know,
in this sort of modern GOP,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.632
the very fact that
she's willing to utter,

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:16.035
you know, the fact that he's
a fallible candidate makes her,

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.904
I guess, singular
at this stage of the game.

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:23.676
I don't think it's possible
to win in the Republican primary

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.344
unless you are Donald Trump.
-Yeah.

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:29.915
-I really think that, you know,
for her to have gone

00:02:29.915 --> 00:02:34.586
to be full-throated consistently
as a critic of Donald Trump

00:02:34.586 --> 00:02:36.922
would have disqualified her
even earlier, you know,

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:38.824
and I think we saw that
with Chris Christie

00:02:38.824 --> 00:02:41.327
and anyone else
who even semi sort of tried.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:45.231
-So now she's in a situation
where maybe she tries to hang on

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:49.501
because she is running against
somebody who has 91 indictments.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.137
He could be in a situation
where, who knows.

00:02:52.137 --> 00:02:53.973
-The rapture, as we call it.
-Absolutely.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:57.210
-The rapture may come, yeah.
-There's never been a candidate

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:59.112
where there seems like
there's more reasons

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.446
he might have to step aside.

00:03:00.446 --> 00:03:02.314
Does she play the long game now
and stick around --

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:04.850
even though, let's be honest,
she's not going to win a state?

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:07.620
-No.
I mean, she will have some...

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:10.022
She will have some electors
to her name.

00:03:10.022 --> 00:03:12.024
DeSantis I think
has like four or five.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:14.794
She's the only person who could
theoretically take the crown

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:16.462
if he's convicted.

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:20.199
But, I mean, I'm hesitant
to get people's hopes up,

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:22.034
people who are not detractors
of Donald Trump,

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:24.837
that somehow Nikki Haley
could pull this thing out.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:28.040
I mean, it would really have
to be a rapture-like scenario.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.044
I see the numbers that,
you know, a sizable portion

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:34.113
of the New Hampshire electorate
doesn't think Donald Trump

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:37.650
is fit to be president
if he's convicted.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.553
But, like, we've got
a long way to go before,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.889
A, there's a trial,
B, there's a conviction

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.857
and the appeals process is over.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.592
And Donald Trump
is going to spend

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:48.728
a lot of time
on the courtroom steps,

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:51.563
spinning this all up
into a partisan witch hunt.

00:03:51.563 --> 00:03:55.801
And the Republican electorate
has proven very permeable

00:03:55.801 --> 00:03:57.269
to that kind of argument.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:59.939
-Well, that's a good
point about exit polls.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:04.143
It does seem that is a very easy
way to voice your frustration

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:06.045
and say "I will not
support this candidate."

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:07.913
And then all of a sudden
it's a general election,

00:04:07.913 --> 00:04:10.216
and there's only
one candidate left

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:11.483
who supports your party.

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:13.785
Do you buy the people
who say this on the way

00:04:13.785 --> 00:04:16.689
out of the polling booth
that they'll never support him?

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:18.023
Or do you think they do
come around?

00:04:18.023 --> 00:04:21.493
-I mean, I think there are --
there are some people

00:04:21.493 --> 00:04:22.928
left in the Republican Party --

00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:24.563
I don't know why they're still
in the Republican Party,

00:04:24.563 --> 00:04:27.099
to be honest -- that still care
about democracy and integrity.

00:04:27.099 --> 00:04:28.534
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.370
-Then I think there's some
people that are asked,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.204
like, when they're coming
out of voting,

00:04:32.204 --> 00:04:34.573
"Hey, do you think the president
should be a convict?"

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:38.077
And they're like, "No,"
because I think

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:39.345
that there's really
a disconnect

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:42.381
between that
sort of moral assessment

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:44.817
of what kind of character
we want from our president

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:48.487
and the reality of that being
Donald Trump, like, their guy.

00:04:48.487 --> 00:04:51.924
And I think you're gonna see --
I don't like to be

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:55.227
a, you know, prognosticator,
but I'm in the business of it.

00:04:55.227 --> 00:04:58.431
Uh, and I would imagine
you're going to see

00:04:58.431 --> 00:05:00.533
that number shrink a little bit
just because of what I said,

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:03.001
like just atrophy, exhaustion,

00:05:03.001 --> 00:05:05.104
Donald Trump
is going to spin this thing.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.572
And then when it comes down
to brass tacks,

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.641
like,
what's the conviction, right?

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:10.676
Is it Stormy Daniels hush money?

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:12.311
Is it Mar-A-Lago documents?

00:05:12.311 --> 00:05:14.113
Is it a federal election
interference case?

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:16.682
I think that all matters as well
in terms of people saying

00:05:16.682 --> 00:05:18.584
"I'm not going to vote
for this dude."

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.353
-Now, obviously we're
in a situation

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:22.422
where I think the, you know,

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.657
the Democratic
electorate is worried.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.325
There was a nervousness that
I think --

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:28.493
-You think?
-I do. I do.

00:05:28.493 --> 00:05:31.263
But, I mean, I guess
there -- This comes back to it.

00:05:31.263 --> 00:05:33.266
There just seems to be less
of a Republican Party

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:35.868
as there is just Donald Trump.
-It's a cult of personality.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.871
-So there -- I guess we're not
going to see Republicans

00:05:38.871 --> 00:05:42.641
freaking out in the same way,
because there are no Republicans

00:05:42.641 --> 00:05:44.376
in the way we classically
think about it anymore

00:05:44.376 --> 00:05:45.177
that matter, right?

00:05:45.177 --> 00:05:46.511
It's Nikki Haley,

00:05:46.511 --> 00:05:49.448
but I also believe that
if he turned around tomorrow

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:51.684
and asked her to be
his vice president,

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.019
I think she'd say yes.
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:55.287
Well, the devotion to Trump
is so singular

00:05:55.287 --> 00:05:57.323
as to be almost
a religion, right?

00:05:57.323 --> 00:05:59.192
So nothing else matters but him.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:01.293
I mean, the only policy proposal

00:06:01.293 --> 00:06:03.262
or the only policy he's
talked about is immigration,

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.397
which really feeds
on xenophobia and racism

00:06:05.397 --> 00:06:08.534
more than a desire to fix
our broken immigration system.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.536
So, yeah, I mean, I think
for them it is

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.905
the end all, be all is Trump and
nothing else matters.

00:06:12.905 --> 00:06:14.406
For Biden, you know, look,

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:16.108
I think there is a lot of
trepidation

00:06:16.108 --> 00:06:17.409
and concern about his age.

00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:19.745
But, like, let's be real,

00:06:19.745 --> 00:06:23.248
Biden has done a bang-up job
with the economy.

00:06:23.248 --> 00:06:24.650
He has canceled
student loan debt.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.953
He canceled more student
loan debt last week.

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:29.555
He has done more on climate than
any other American president.

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:31.990
I mean, his record,
given a one-seat majority

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:34.159
in the Senate, is bonkers.

00:06:34.159 --> 00:06:37.096
And the fact that the dude
is old should not erase

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:39.565
what is a formidable record for
his first three years in office.

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.601
-I agree.

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:45.771
What is the problem?

00:06:45.771 --> 00:06:47.406
Why do you feel
like that message

00:06:47.406 --> 00:06:49.842
is, one, maybe not effectively
getting out,

00:06:49.842 --> 00:06:53.345
and, two, even when it's getting
out, not resonating with people?

00:06:53.345 --> 00:06:54.580
-Vibes, Seth.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.516
I've been told
it's the TikTok vibes.

00:06:57.516 --> 00:06:59.018
-Yeah.
-But the vibes are changing.

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:01.254
I mean, the metrics
about consumer confidence

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:04.356
have gone up
I think like 15% to 20%

00:07:04.356 --> 00:07:07.326
in the last couple of weeks,
so that's a good indicator

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:09.228
that maybe people
are finally catching on.

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:10.763
Part of it is narrative.

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:14.200
Part of it is miseducation
and redirection.

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.667
You know,
inflation's coming down.

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:19.539
I think that's the clearest,
most sort of pinpointable reason

00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:21.340
why people don't feel
like the economy is good

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.910
because job creation, wages,
like, that stuff

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:26.812
is doing well
for almost everybody.

00:07:26.812 --> 00:07:28.113
And I'm not even talking
about the stock market,

00:07:28.113 --> 00:07:29.248
'cause that's not
most Americans.

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:30.716
But that thing is booming.

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:33.386
So, I mean,
I'm not a Biden spokesperson,

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:34.787
but I think, look,

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:37.189
there's a long way to go
between now and November,

00:07:37.189 --> 00:07:38.958
and people's opinions
can change.

00:07:38.958 --> 00:07:40.258
There could be
black swan events.

00:07:40.258 --> 00:07:42.595
The rapture could come.
-Yeah.

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:46.164
-People feel differently about
this country month to month.

00:07:46.164 --> 00:07:48.434
And the Biden team
is betting that people

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:50.469
are going to feel better
about the economy,

00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:53.105
their place therein,
and feel a lot worse

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:55.608
about a narcissistic,
potentially convicted felon

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:57.243
being elected into office.
-It's not a

00:07:57.243 --> 00:07:59.878
bad long-term plan.
-Yeah, I mean...

00:07:59.878 --> 00:08:01.614
-So on a personal level,

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:03.448
you obviously -- you get to,

00:08:03.448 --> 00:08:04.783
you know,
work on election night.

00:08:04.783 --> 00:08:07.320
As you said, called an hour in,
not very dramatic.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.721
Do you feel any heartache
about the fact that

00:08:09.721 --> 00:08:12.357
you're not going to have sort of
a breathless primary season

00:08:12.357 --> 00:08:15.828
of the horse-race politics
that do make good television,

00:08:15.828 --> 00:08:17.229
but you're just not
going to get it?

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:19.498
-I know.
I mean, eating pizza,

00:08:19.498 --> 00:08:21.100
cold pizza at 11:30 at night

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.268
with, like, under-eye concealer
flaking off your face.

00:08:23.268 --> 00:08:25.237
I'm going to miss it.

00:08:25.237 --> 00:08:29.007
No, it is -- Actually,
I am a little sad, not just --

00:08:29.007 --> 00:08:31.477
I mean, let me just say, like,
the lament of the TV host.

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:32.878
Like, I don't get
to sit there on set

00:08:32.878 --> 00:08:34.179
and make the big party happen.

00:08:34.179 --> 00:08:36.314
I feel bad for democracy.

00:08:36.314 --> 00:08:39.985
Like, it's a good -- Like,
200,000 people have voted.

00:08:39.985 --> 00:08:42.087
We're a country of over
300 million people.

00:08:42.087 --> 00:08:43.288
Like, it shouldn't be over now.

00:08:43.288 --> 00:08:45.824
There should be debates
in the general election.

00:08:45.824 --> 00:08:48.193
There should have been debates
in the primary season.

00:08:48.193 --> 00:08:49.495
You know, maybe
it would have been nice

00:08:49.495 --> 00:08:50.896
to have an open
Democratic primary

00:08:50.896 --> 00:08:52.297
given all the misgivings
about Biden.

00:08:52.297 --> 00:08:55.201
But, like, we get stronger
in those moments, not weaker.

00:08:55.201 --> 00:08:57.036
And it's sad to me that
we're not going to have any...

00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:58.370
-I agree with you 100%.

00:08:58.370 --> 00:09:00.906
It does feel like we've all
just sort of checked out

00:09:00.906 --> 00:09:01.807
on this idea.

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:02.975
And then people say, "You know,

00:09:02.975 --> 00:09:04.376
I'm not really happy
with the two choices."

00:09:04.376 --> 00:09:06.212
And you're like,
"Yeah, it's not..."

00:09:06.212 --> 00:09:08.013
-Well,
as Rachel said last night,

00:09:08.013 --> 00:09:09.181
there's not a lot of democracy

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:10.583
going on in this democracy
right now.

00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:12.084
-Yeah. Well, we should get
some more democracy in here.

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:13.419
-Yeah. Well, can
someone bring it in?

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:14.920
-Alright, you and I,
let's get down to it.

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.455
-Bang.
-Thank you for being here.

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:18.657
It's always so good to see you.
Alex Wagner, everybody.

00:09:18.657 --> 00:09:21.026
"Alex Wagner Tonight" airs
Tuesdays through Fridays

00:09:21.026 --> 00:09:22.395
at 9 p.m. on MSNBC.

00:09:22.395 --> 00:09:25.197
We'll be right back
with J. Smith-Cameron.

